PCI: ACPI: keep the ACPI companion of a bridge that has a device-tree node

openHC's EA boards (Intel CE5300) boot with ACPI and link a device tree into
the kernel (patch 0015) to describe board devices behind the CE5300 A/V bridge
00:01.0: GPIO hogs and names, the I2C devices, the SPI switch, the USB VBUS
supply. Bus 1 only gets an OF node through that bridge's node, so the bridge
must be in the tree. pci_set_of_node() then gives it an OF fwnode, and
pci_set_acpi_fwnode() skips attaching its ACPI companion. That companion
(\_SB.PCI0.PCI1 in CEFDK's DSDT) holds the _PRT for bus 1, so without it
every device there comes up "PCI INT x: no GSI" (measured on an EA3: gpio,
spi, i2c, e1000, sdhci, ehci, the i2s).

Attach the companion to a bridge that has an OF node, and keep the node as
of_node only. That is how device_add_of_node() attaches a node the PCI core
creates (PCI_DYNAMIC_OF_NODES), and pci_set_bus_of_node() reads of_node, so
the bus below still inherits the tree. A bridge without a companion keeps
its OF fwnode, and nothing changes for any device that is not a bridge.

On the EA no device on bus 1 has a companion of its own: CEFDK's DSDT names
them with wildcard _ADRs (0x000CFFFF etc.), which never match. So their
fwnode stays the OF node and their drivers keep reading the tree.

Replaces the earlier 0017, which looked the bridge's ACPI node up by _ADR in
drivers/acpi/pci_irq.c instead.

Author: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
--- a/drivers/pci/pci-acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pci-acpi.c
@@ -945,9 +945,27 @@
 
 void pci_set_acpi_fwnode(struct pci_dev *dev)
 {
-	if (!dev_fwnode(&dev->dev) && !pci_dev_is_added(dev))
+	struct acpi_device *adev;
+
+	if (pci_dev_is_added(dev))
+		return;
+
+	if (!dev_fwnode(&dev->dev)) {
 		ACPI_COMPANION_SET(&dev->dev,
 				   acpi_pci_find_companion(&dev->dev));
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * A bridge with a device tree node still needs its ACPI companion,
+	 * which holds the _PRT for the bus below. Keep the node as of_node
+	 * only, as device_add_of_node() does; the bus below inherits that.
+	 */
+	if (pci_is_bridge(dev) && dev_of_node(&dev->dev)) {
+		adev = acpi_pci_find_companion(&dev->dev);
+		if (adev)
+			ACPI_COMPANION_SET(&dev->dev, adev);
+	}
 }
 
